{%- doc -%}
  The problem, and the sentence that answers it.

  Two lines, always in that order, because a product page that opens with what
  the thing is asks the reader to work out why they should care. A page that
  opens with the reader's own problem has already earned the next sentence.

  Both lines come from the product, so every page gets its own pair and none of
  it is written into the theme. A product missing either line renders nothing
  rather than half a pair, which would read as a mistake.

  @param {product} product
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign ps_problem = product.metafields.custom.problem_line.value
  assign ps_solution = product.metafields.custom.solution_line.value
-%}

{%- if ps_problem != blank and ps_solution != blank -%}
  <div class="pl-ps">
    <p class="pl-ps__line pl-ps__line--problem">
      <span class="pl-ps__tag">הבעיה</span>
      <span class="pl-ps__text">{{ ps_problem }}</span>
    </p>
    <p class="pl-ps__line pl-ps__line--solution">
      <span class="pl-ps__tag">הפתרון</span>
      <span class="pl-ps__text">{{ ps_solution }}</span>
    </p>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
